<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Slowdown in farmer sales.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Slowdown in farmer sales.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farmer sales of spring wheat were at a virtual standstill on Monday as a decline in MGE futures values prompted producers to review their options, merchandisers said.</p>
<p>Sales picked up early last week as the market started to rally after a long slide but the respite proved short-lived with prices dipping on Friday and Monday. Dec MGE spring wheat futures closed six cents a bushel lower at $3.98-1/4 on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It was very quiet with the board (futures) being down. Producers are taking time to think,&quot; one Montana based merchandiser said.  </p>
